The memory the processes of every object of this namespace, taken together,
may use before the kernel slows them down, reclaiming their memory and
throttling their allocations, in bytes.

Unlike `pg_mem_limit`, reaching it does not wake the Out-Of-Memory killer: a
namespace above it keeps running, slower, while the kernel reclaims. Only the
unified cgroup hierarchy has it.

Setting this keyword to `default` puts the capping back where a node that
never capped anything leaves it. Removing the keyword does not: what was
written stays written, whether om wrote it or something else did.
